    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0568" n="478" xml:id="pg478"/>

                <head>No. 232.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Bartholdi.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-02-23"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 23,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note under date of the
                    4th January last, requesting this Government to use its good offices with that
                    of Mexico, with a view to having the time fixed for the expulsion of the Sisters
                    of Charity from that country extended to the present month, I have now the honor
                    to inclose herewith, for your information, copy of dispatch No.:239,<anchor
                        n="*" xml:id="d236-f1"/> addressed to this Department by the minister of the
                    United States in Mexico, to whom the matter was referred.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d236-f1" n="*" xml:id="d236-f1-content">
                <p>See under “Mexico.”</p>
            </note>
